From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:52:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Tell a group's own news in words

A group just made opened with "Unsupported message type" and TDLib's
description of messageBasicGroupChatCreate, since that message is what
starts its chat; members joining, leaving, being added or removed, and
a pinned message came in the same way.

They are now notices: "X created Physics", "X added A, B", "X joined",
"X joined by an invite link", "X left", "X removed Y", "X pinned a
message". Members are named as TDLib has given their names, and
"Unknown user" where it has not yet. An anonymous channel post names
nobody ("Physics was created", "A message was pinned").

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/UnitedMarsupials/tdlib-purple/pull/35]
---
